<!--Post: 3694--><!--Time: 1105139829-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3694"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:Iwillc@tchu.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Catcher<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Catcher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 3:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has anyone else thought of the fact that BTK could be visiting the gravesites of his victims on or near anniversary dates?  It is my understanding that the Otero family members were honored for burial in Puerto Rico.  I don&#39;t know if BTK would go that far, but perhaps here in Wichita?  Does anyone know of the locations of the deceased loved ones buried here in Wichita?  I hope this doesn&#39;t break any posting rules, but I don&#39;t recall seeing anyone touch on this possibility yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3694-->
<!--Post: 3697--><!--Time: 1105140132-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3697"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 3:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That is a good question.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3697-->
<!--Post: 3699--><!--Time: 1105140343-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3699"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jujuree<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jujuree<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 3:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That is a good question, Catcher.  I wonder if the WPD has ever done surveillance on a victim&#39;s grave, just to see? <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think the WPD would have the resources to keep doing that if it didn&#39;t pan out after a few tries, but I do think that could be worth a try. <BR> <BR>&#40;Well, maybe not now if BTK reads this board! LOL&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3699-->
<!--Post: 3712--><!--Time: 1105149948-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3712"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 6:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I bet that BTK has done this, probably at night, especially during the extended period when many thought him deceased or forever moved away. I can also see him visiting graves during daylight. &#40;Although not anymore; in fact, among his fantasy fodder might be gravesite pictures.&#41;  I wonder if he&#39;s submitted any gravesite photos or headstone impressions? BTK isn&#39;t brilliant but I&#39;d bet he&#39;d be savvy enough to have an ancillary reason for being at the gravesite should someone ask him why he&#39;s there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3712-->
<!--Post: 3788--><!--Time: 1105232209-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 4:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In NJ there was a man who killed his family on the run for 17 years &amp; police would visit the grave every year on the aniversity waiting for the man to visit. Later he was caught on AMW &#40;John List&#41; &amp; he never once visited the graves all those years we found out. But he was also did not live anywere near NJ during all of those years .<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3788-->
<!--Post: 6001--><!--Time: 1107477257-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6001"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Purple<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Purple<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 4:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just out of curiosity, I typed &#34;Otero Family&#34; in GOOGLE to see what would come up.  I found the website, findagrave.com, I think that is correct.  Anyway, they show that the Otero&#39;s are buried on Bayamon, Puerto Rico in the National Cemetery.  Shows where the graves are, not the headstones and also pictures of Joseph and Julie.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6001-->
<!--Post: 6035--><!--Time: 1107486608-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6035"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 7:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->very interesting Info. Thank for sharing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6035-->
